      "data": {
        "text": "\"Build the service integrations for a realistic text-to-speech task set with same-scenario integration files, local helper files, and later-step integration files.\nThe initial file synthesize_text.py is already implemented. Read it before generating the remaining files, and leave it unchanged.\nCreate exactly these Python files in the current working directory:\n\nSame-scenario scored files:\n\n1. [SAME-SCENARIO] synthesize_text.py - synthesizes plain text to an audio byte stream\n2. [SAME-SCENARIO] synthesize_ssml.py - synthesizes SSML with voice and prosody controls\n3. [SAME-SCENARIO] select_voice.py - lists or selects a voice for a target locale\n4. [SAME-SCENARIO] save_audio.py - writes synthesized speech audio to a local file or object\n\nLocal helper files:\n\n5. [HELPER] speech_client.py - Provide local configuration and client helper utilities for Text-to-Speech\n6. [HELPER] speech_models.py - Define local request, response, and normalization helpers for Text-to-Speech\n\nLater-step scored files:\n\n7. [LATER-STEP] script_translate.py - Translate narration scripts before synthesis\n8. [LATER-STEP] script_safety.py - Check narration scripts for unsafe content\n9. [LATER-STEP] script_embedding.py - Embed narration scripts for voice-asset search\n10. [LATER-STEP] tts_qa_transcript.py - Transcribe synthesized QA samples to verify spoken output\n\nRequirements:\n- Scored implementation files are the listed [SAME-SCENARIO] and [LATER-STEP] files when those labels are shown.\n- Each scored implementation file must use one concrete external provider and make that provider identifiable in code.\n- Write exactly the listed files in the current working directory. Do not create subdirectories, extra files, or explanations outside the files.\n- The local helper files may contain configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities when useful.\"",
        "type": "text"
      },
